{
 "id": "1ch-8-benjamin",
 "title": "The Family of Benjamin",
 "ref": "1 Chronicles 8:1–28",
 "intro": [
  "A second, longer genealogy of Benjamin, the tribe of Saul and, with Judah, the heart of the post-exilic community. It names the families of Geba, of Ono and Lod, of Aijalon, and those who \"lived in Jerusalem\" (8:28). Saul's family, which follows (8:29–40), has its own tree.",
  "Several links between these families are not stated; a dashed line marks them."
 ],
 "col": "plum",
 "sources": "Hebrew names: Miqra according to the Masorah. Scholarly summary after the standard commentaries (Japhet; Williamson; Knoppers).",
 "anchor": {
